is the basis for distributed execution, dynamic transformation, and queries over the running program itself; zero-copy cross-device migration is the UCF design target rather than a completed feature.\"]]]\n\u001b[031m-          \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n           [:details.faq\n            [:summary \"If a running program (a continuation) is saved to the database and moved to a completely different machine, do the internal memory IDs clash? Do I have to manually rewrite them ('parallel transport')?\"]\n            [:div\n--- a/public/chp/dao-lease.chp\n+++ b/public/chp/dao-lease.chp\n\u001b[036m@@ -25,102 +25,102 @@\u001b[0m\n           \"and the judge is a step function embedded in the process that possesses the resource, \"\n           \"driven by that process's own loop. Anyone may reach a conclusion about a lease. \"\n           \"Only the possessor's conclusion has effect, because only the possessor can actually take the resource back.\"]]\n\u001b[031m-       [:section#how.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-        [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:h2 \"How a lease lives and dies\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A holder that has not observed a grantor-authored grant holds nothing. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Once it has, it renews at strictly less than half the granted duration, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"measured against readings on its own tick stream. A renewal is an append that answers ok; \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"any other outcome advances no bound. The holder stops acting at its bound whether or not anything has been heard, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and releases when done, which spares the grantor a full duration of waiting.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The judge keeps a private ledger of live grants and runs a pass at a declared cadence. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Each pass drains its tick cursor (that reading is now, never a clock call), drains the lease-fact cursors, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"answers proposals, classifies every lease by the first cause that holds, reclaims, and only then records. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The record follows the act: an absent :lapsed fact is never evidence of tenure. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A lease is due for reclaim by the first cause that holds, in this order:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:table.principles-table\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:thead\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-           [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:th \"Cause\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:th \"Meaning\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:tbody\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-           [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \":release\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \"The holder said it was done. The reclaim is still the grantor's act; the release just spares everyone a duration of waiting.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-           [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \":silence\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \"No eligible renewal was observed within duration plus tolerance, over a window the judge actually observed.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-           [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \":cap\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \"Total tenure passed the grant's maximum. Renewals cannot help: a hostile or wedged holder cannot squat forever.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-           [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \":policy\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-            [:td \"The grantor's own reason to end it early. A policy may end a lease, but it may not be implemented by declining to count eligible evidence.\"]]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The four causes are ordered: a lease already pending its reclaim keeps its cause, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"a release wins before the cap, the cap before policy, and silence comes last. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Reclamation is bounded by duration plus tolerance plus cadence plus the cost of the reclaim itself.\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-       [:section#authority.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-        [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:h2 \"Facts can be forged. Leases cannot.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A lease fact is an unauthenticated map, and anyone who can append to a medium can write one. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"So the security never rests on the fact. It rests on three gates the fact cannot cross by forgery:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Attribution first: every fact passes through a composition-supplied resolver bound to the medium it was read from, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and only facts the resolver attributes to the right party count. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A forged renewal in the holder's name counts for nothing: silence is measured as though it never arrived. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A forged release establishes nothing, and cannot pre-empt the genuine holder's later one. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"A forged grant seeds no tenure: only the judge's own grants do that.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Registration second: a lease connects to a medium only through an authoritative fact, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"so an attacker's own noisy medium cannot be attached to someone else's lease, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and flooding it manufactures no evidence.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Possession third: a forged :lapsed records nothing, because recording follows a successful reclaim, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and only the possessor can perform the reclaim. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The resource itself is the ground truth: a remote holder learns of a reclaim by observing it, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"not by trusting anyone's broadcast.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"And when the medium breaks its promise, by evicting facts before the judge read them, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"the judge does not guess. The lease's evidence state becomes unknown, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and the judge demands a full clean duration of observation before silence counts again. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Weaker evidence may delay a conclusion. It must never accelerate one.\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-       [:section#uses.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-        [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:h2 \"Three uses, and the refusals\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The vocabulary is scoped to three sanctioned uses: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"the pause a reader holds over a forwarder, the lifetime of a served connection, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and the claim an agent leaves on shared work. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"It is deliberately silent about everything else:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:ul\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:li \"No delegated renewal: a renewal is evidence about its own author. Delegation is a chain of ordinary leases, each with its own judge.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:li \"No transfer between holders: renegotiate instead.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:li \"No absolute time in any fact: durations cross boundaries, moments never do.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:li \"No access enforcement: the bound bounds attention, not access. A holder needing real exclusion obtains it from the resource, through fencing.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"Sizing is stated as relations and the values belong to compositions: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"the granted duration exceeds twice the renewal interval, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"the tolerance covers flight time and clock skew, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"the renewal interval plus one tick period stays below half the duration, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and a medium's retention window exceeds the judge's lag. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The contract, the rationale, and the implementation are on GitHub: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/blob/master/docs/design/dao.lease.md\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"dao.lease.md\"] \", \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/blob/master/docs/design/dao.lease.rationale.md\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"dao.lease.rationale.md\"] \", \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and the implementation under \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/tree/master/src/cljc/dao\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"src/cljc/dao\"] \".\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"The deeper lineage is written down too. The judge is a garbage collector for claims: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"it reclaims what a silent holder no longer proves it wants, the way a collector reclaims what the \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"execution log no longer reaches. That unification, where JIT, GC, and this judge become three \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"interpreters of the same stream, is the subject of \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"/blog/unification-of-jit-and-gc.blog\"} \"The Unification of JIT and GC\"] \".\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-         [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"DaoLease pairs with the rest of the stack: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"/dao-stream.chp\"} \"DaoStream\"] \" carries the facts, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"/dao-space.chp\"} \"DaoSpace\"] \" makes them queryable, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          [:a {:href \"/shibi.chp\"} \"Shibi\"] \" confines untrusted computation, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-          \"and DaoLease decides whose turn it is.\"]]]])} template))\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+        [:section#how.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+         [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:h2 \"How a lease lives and dies\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A holder that has not observed a grantor-authored grant holds nothing. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Once it has, it renews at strictly less than half the granted duration, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"measured against readings on its own tick stream. A renewal is an append that answers ok; \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"any other outcome advances no bound. The holder stops acting at its bound whether or not anything has been heard, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and releases when done, which spares the grantor a full duration of waiting.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The judge keeps a private ledger of live grants and runs a pass at a declared cadence. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Each pass drains its tick cursor (that reading is now, never a clock call), drains the lease-fact cursors, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"answers proposals, classifies every lease by the first cause that holds, reclaims, and only then records. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The record follows the act: an absent :lapsed fact is never evidence of tenure. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A lease is due for reclaim by the first cause that holds, in this order:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:table.principles-table\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:thead\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+            [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:th \"Cause\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:th \"Meaning\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:tbody\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+            [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \":release\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \"The holder said it was done. The reclaim is still the grantor's act; the release just spares everyone a duration of waiting.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+            [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \":silence\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \"No eligible renewal was observed within duration plus tolerance, over a window the judge actually observed.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+            [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \":cap\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \"Total tenure passed the grant's maximum. Renewals cannot help: a hostile or wedged holder cannot squat forever.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+            [:tr\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \":policy\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+             [:td \"The grantor's own reason to end it early. A policy may end a lease, but it may not be implemented by declining to count eligible evidence.\"]]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The four causes are ordered: a lease already pending its reclaim keeps its cause, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"a release wins before the cap, the cap before policy, and silence comes last. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Reclamation is bounded by duration plus tolerance plus cadence plus the cost of the reclaim itself.\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+        [:section#authority.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+         [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:h2 \"Facts can be forged. Leases cannot.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A lease fact is an unauthenticated map, and anyone who can append to a medium can write one. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"So the security never rests on the fact. It rests on three gates the fact cannot cross by forgery:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Attribution first: every fact passes through a composition-supplied resolver bound to the medium it was read from, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and only facts the resolver attributes to the right party count. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A forged renewal in the holder's name counts for nothing: silence is measured as though it never arrived. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A forged release establishes nothing, and cannot pre-empt the genuine holder's later one. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"A forged grant seeds no tenure: only the judge's own grants do that.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Registration second: a lease connects to a medium only through an authoritative fact, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"so an attacker's own noisy medium cannot be attached to someone else's lease, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and flooding it manufactures no evidence.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Possession third: a forged :lapsed records nothing, because recording follows a successful reclaim, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and only the possessor can perform the reclaim. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The resource itself is the ground truth: a remote holder learns of a reclaim by observing it, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"not by trusting anyone's broadcast.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"And when the medium breaks its promise, by evicting facts before the judge read them, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"the judge does not guess. The lease's evidence state becomes unknown, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and the judge demands a full clean duration of observation before silence counts again. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Weaker evidence may delay a conclusion. It must never accelerate one.\"]]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+        [:section#uses.section-dark\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+         [:div.section-inner\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:h2 \"Three uses, and the refusals\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The vocabulary is scoped to three sanctioned uses: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"the pause a reader holds over a forwarder, the lifetime of a served connection, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and the claim an agent leaves on shared work. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"It is deliberately silent about everything else:\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:ul\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:li \"No delegated renewal: a renewal is evidence about its own author. Delegation is a chain of ordinary leases, each with its own judge.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:li \"No transfer between holders: renegotiate instead.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:li \"No absolute time in any fact: durations cross boundaries, moments never do.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:li \"No access enforcement: the bound bounds attention, not access. A holder needing real exclusion obtains it from the resource, through fencing.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"Sizing is stated as relations and the values belong to compositions: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"the granted duration exceeds twice the renewal interval, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"the tolerance covers flight time and clock skew, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"the renewal interval plus one tick period stays below half the duration, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and a medium's retention window exceeds the judge's lag. \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The contract, the rationale, and the implementation are on GitHub: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/blob/master/docs/design/dao.lease.md\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"dao.lease.md\"] \", \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/blob/master/docs/design/dao.lease.rationale.md\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"dao.lease.rationale.md\"] \", \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and the implementation under \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"https://github.com/sonwh98/datomworld/tree/master/src/cljc/dao\" :target \"_blank\" :rel \"noopener noreferrer\"} \"src/cljc/dao\"] \".\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"The deeper lineage is written down too. The judge is a garbage collector for claims: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"it reclaims what a silent holder no longer proves it wants, the way a collector reclaims what the \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"execution log no longer reaches. That unification, where JIT, GC, and this judge become three \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"interpreters of the same stream, is the subject of \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"/blog/unification-of-jit-and-gc.blog\"} \"The Unification of JIT and GC\"] \".\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+          [:p\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"DaoLease pairs with the rest of the stack: \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"/dao-stream.chp\"} \"DaoStream\"] \" carries the facts, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"/dao-space.chp\"} \"DaoSpace\"] \" makes them queryable, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           [:a {:href \"/shibi.chp\"} \"Shibi\"] \" confines untrusted computation, \"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"and DaoLease decides whose turn it is.\"]]]])} template))\u001b[0m\n--- a/src/dev/affected.clj\n+++ b/src/dev/affected.clj\n\u001b[036m@@ -369,6 +369,7 @@\u001b[0m\n               test-nses\n               (into #{} (mapcat :tests) (vals reasons)))}))\n \n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n (def subsystems-config-path \"src/dev/subsystems.edn\")\n \n \n--- a/deps.edn\n+++ b/deps.edn\n\u001b[036m@@ -55,8 +55,7 @@\u001b[0m\n            ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n            :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n                                       {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n\u001b[031m-                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                                      }}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}}}\u001b[0m\n            :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n                   :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n--- a/antlr/python3/manifest.edn\n+++ b/antlr/python3/manifest.edn\n\u001b[036m@@ -60,3 +60,4 @@\u001b[0m\n                                      \"antlr/python3/Python3Parser.g4\"],\n                   :generated-artifacts :none,\n                   :blocked-until \"Java helper provenance and licence resolved\"}}\n\u001b[031m-\u001b[0m\n--- a/public/chp/blog/universal-ast-vs-assembly.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/universal-ast-vs-assembly.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@\u001b[0m\n            [:code\n             \"; Adding two numbers\\nMOV R1, #5\\nMOV R2, #3\\nADD R3, R1, R2\\n\\n; Adding two other numbers\\nMOV R4, #10\\nMOV R5, #7\\nADD R6, R4, R5\"]]\n           [:p\n\u001b[031m-           \"You cannot easily ask an assembly file: \"Find all call sites of addition.\" You would have to parse raw opcodes, reconstruct control-flow graphs, and guess register lifespans.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+           \"You cannot easily ask an assembly file: \" Find all call sites of addition. \" You would have to parse raw opcodes, reconstruct control-flow graphs, and guess register lifespans.\"]\u001b[0m\n           [:p\n            \"Because the Universal AST projects into structured semantic tuples, it is queryable with Datalog in \"\n            [:a {:href \"/dao-space.chp\"} \"DaoSpace\"]\n\u001b[036m@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@\u001b[0m\n  [?app :yin/operator ?op]\n  [?op :yin/name +]]\n \n\u001b[031m-;; Find all variable references to parameter \"count\"\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+;; Find all variable references to parameter \" count \"\u001b[0m\n [:find ?node\n  :where\n  [?node :yin/type :variable]\n--- a/public/chp/blog/io-monad-dao-stream.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/io-monad-dao-stream.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -6,42 +6,39 @@\u001b[0m\n                   [:article\n                    :$blog-title\n                    :$blog-date\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"In pure functional programming, the IO monad solves a critical problem: how to perform dirty side effects while keeping core logic pure. When a Haskell program returns an IO action, it does not actually execute the network request. It returns a pure, first-class value denoting the effect (well-defined, but not a data structure). The language runtime, acting as the host boundary, takes that value and executes it.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"Conceptually, this is elegant. Practically, standard IO keeps the effect out of the program's reach: an IO value is well-defined, but it is not data. It can be composed or handed to the runtime to be executed; it cannot be taken apart to see the next effect before it runs. For a general action, that description does not even exist until execution computes it. There is no Eq, no Show, no pattern matching: nothing exposes the pending effect as data. The only thing that can run an IO value is the runtime itself (unsafePerformIO is the sanctioned exception).\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:h2 \"IO is Just State Awaiting an Interpreter\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"To understand why this opacity is a limitation, it is necessary to look at the underlying mechanics. Structurally, the IO monad and the State monad are the exact same shape. In Clojure terms, the State monad is just a pure function that takes an immutable value (like a map), and returns a result alongside an updated map. The interpreter lives \" [:em \"inside\"] \" the program: evaluating the function allows inspecting the resulting data structure.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"The IO monad operates identically, but the \\\"state\\\" it threads is a phantom token representing the physical universe. Because pure functions cannot directly mutate the outside world, the interpreter must live \" [:em \"outside\"] \" the language as a privileged host environment. The pure program simply builds a sequence of transitions over this dummy token, and the external host acts as the sole interpreter permitted to execute the actual side-effects. The intent is executed, but the data describing it is swallowed by the runtime.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:h2 \"From Opaque Actions to Transparent Syntax\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"The datom.world architecture rejects opaque abstractions. The core philosophy is that everything is data, and that data is syntax. Semantics only emerge through interpretation.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"In \" [:code \"yin.vm\"] \", the virtual machine for executing portable code, IO is handled using this exact IO Monad pattern, but without the opacity. When a continuation in \" [:code \"yin.vm\"] \" needs to interact with the outside world (like writing to a stream or mutating a cell), it does not actually perform the side-effect. As implemented in the VM's source code, pure functions simply return an effect constructor (via \" [:code \"make-effect\"] \"). Rather than yielding an opaque runtime type, the continuation emits a literal, inspectable plain-data effect descriptor. The VM engine then acts as the outer interpreter that reads and executes these returned effects.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"Because a host boundary is a stream boundary, never a function call, the agent code completely detaches from the execution. It simply appends its intent to the stream and pauses.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:h2 \"Stigmergic Coordination\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"Forcing side effects to exist as transparent, plain data on a stream unlocks stigmergic coordination. A stream has no privileged reader. Because the intent is just syntax, multiple independent interpreters can observe it simultaneously:\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:ul\n                     [:li \"The host adapter reads the descriptor and performs the actual physical network request.\"]\n                     [:li \"An audit interpreter can read the exact same descriptor and record it for compliance.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                    [:li \"A test interpreter intercepts the descriptor and injects a mock response back onto the stream, never touching the physical network.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                    [:li \"A test interpreter intercepts the descriptor and injects a mock response back onto the stream, never touching the physical network.\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"If a traditional opaque IO monad were used, the auditor and the test suite would have to be coupled to the execution layer. Turning the IO monad into transparent data on dao.stream lets the system emerge from independent interpreters of pure data.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:h2 \"Related Articles\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:ul\n                     [:li [:a {:href \"/blog/monads.blog\"} \"The History and Architecture of Monads: From Category Theory to Clojure\"]]\n                     [:li [:a {:href \"/blog/the-cesk-machine-control-environment-store-continuation.blog\"} \"The CESK Machine: Control, Environment, Store, Continuation\"]]\n\u001b[031m-                    [:li [:a {:href \"/blog/stream-vs-interface-architecture.blog\"} \"Stream vs. Interface Architecture\"]]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]]]}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                    [:li [:a {:href \"/blog/stream-vs-interface-architecture.blog\"} \"Stream vs. Interface Architecture\"]]]]]]}\u001b[0m\n--- a/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-rust-kernel.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-rust-kernel.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -51,5 +51,4 @@\u001b[0m\n \n                    [:p \"The worker is node-local because a receiver cannot validate a native artifact short of rebuilding it. A node runs only artifacts its own worker built from images its own validator admitted, so native artifacts never cross between nodes. What crosses is unchanged: images and continuations as data.\"]\n \n\u001b[031m-                   [:p \"The expected performance gain of this native compilation is bounded and will be measured in a dedicated benchmark phase before any LLVM code is written. A node with no toolchain remains a complete node that interprets, the kernel never waits on the worker, and a native artifact can be dropped at any boundary without changing the outcome.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]]]}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                   [:p \"The expected performance gain of this native compilation is bounded and will be measured in a dedicated benchmark phase before any LLVM code is written. A node with no toolchain remains a complete node that interprets, the kernel never waits on the worker, and a native artifact can be dropped at any boundary without changing the outcome.\"]]]]}\u001b[0m\n--- a/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-macros.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-macros.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -8,14 +8,14 @@\u001b[0m\n                    :$blog-date\n \n                    [:p \"Macros are the defining superpower of Lisp. They allow developers to bend the language to their will, creating domain-specific abstractions that feel native. But this power comes at a steep architectural cost: compile-time environments bleed into runtime, infinite loops crash compilers, and tracking the provenance of generated code is notoriously difficult.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"In datom.world, the yin.vm runtime takes a radical approach to metaprogramming. It achieves the full power of homoiconic Lisp macros by doing something unthinkable: \" [:strong \"it hides macros completely from the evaluator.\"]]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"Here is a look at what makes the yin.vm macro system utterly unique, what it can do that other systems cannot, and how it compares to the macro engines of Clojure, Erlang, Rust, Racket, and Unison.\"]\n \n                    [:h2 \"1. The Evaluator is Macro-Blind\"]\n                    [:p \"In almost every Lisp (like Clojure or Common Lisp), macroexpansion is deeply interleaved with the compiler and evaluator. The engine looks at a symbol, checks if it has a special macro flag, and halts evaluation to execute the macro transformation before continuing.\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   \u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"In yin.vm, \" [:strong \"the evaluator knows absolutely nothing about macros.\"] \" It has no macro instruction, no expansion ledger, and no macro flag on closures. A lambda can be marked as a macro on the syntax side, but that mark is dropped before code reaches the evaluator. Instead, yin.vm models macroexpansion strictly as a \" [:strong \"stream topology\"] \":\"]\n \n                    [:pre \"Frontend -> (program-in) -> Expander -> (program-out) -> Evaluator\"]\n\u001b[036m@@ -63,5 +63,4 @@\u001b[0m\n                    [:p \"While Unison doesn't have a macro system, it shares yin.vm's fundamental philosophy of content-addressed code. Unison stores ASTs in a database by their cryptographic hash rather than in text files, just as yin.vm operates natively on content-addressed row tuples. Unison evaluation never parses text; it evaluates canonical AST structures directly from the store. However, Unison eschews macros entirely, relying on Algebraic Effects for abstraction. yin.vm takes the Unison data-model and proves that you can build a safe, robust macro system on top of it by keeping the transformations confined to the stream layer.\"]\n \n                    [:h2 \"Conclusion\"]\n\u001b[031m-                   [:p \"The brilliance of the yin.vm macro system lies in what it refuses to do. By refusing to let the evaluator know about macros, refusing to let macros access I/O, and refusing to invent complex compiler phases, it distills metaprogramming down to its purest essence: a deterministic, safe, and easily distributed stream of data.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]]]}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                   [:p \"The brilliance of the yin.vm macro system lies in what it refuses to do. By refusing to let the evaluator know about macros, refusing to let macros access I/O, and refusing to invent complex compiler phases, it distills metaprogramming down to its purest essence: a deterministic, safe, and easily distributed stream of data.\"]]]]}\u001b[0m\n--- a/public/chp/blog/why-clojure-has-no-linker.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/why-clojure-has-no-linker.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -97,5 +97,4 @@\u001b[0m\n \n                    [:p \"And because linking is a stream exchange rather than a build phase, none of this costs the REPL. Images stream in over content-addressed storage; new modules install into the running system as they arrive; the dynamics stay dynamic. What changes is that the system can now say no: to a payload that isn't what its address claims, to a dependency that won't bind identically, to a module whose name is a lie.\"]\n \n\u001b[031m-                   [:p \"Clojure has no linker because it never stops loading. We think the fix is not to stop; it is to finally check.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                  ]]]}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                   [:p \"Clojure has no linker because it never stops loading. We think the fix is not to stop; it is to finally check.\"]]]]}\u001b[0m\n--- a/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-vs-unison.blog\n+++ b/public/chp/blog/yin-vm-vs-unison.blog\n\u001b[036m@@ -110,5 +110,4 @@\u001b[0m\n                    [:h2 \"Conclusion\"]\n                    [:p \"Unison hashes a nameless form of each definition, keeps names as separate metadata, and uses that one hash both as identity and as the thing it fetches and runs. \" [:code \"yin.vm\"] \" keeps the names in the source AST, derives a coarse semantic fingerprint and two exact peer executable identities from it, and treats the sharing of those images over \" [:code \"dao.stream\"] \" as the point of the exercise.\"]\n \n\u001b[031m-                   [:p \"Today yin.vm has the named source, the semantic VM, the projection and fingerprint, the De Bruijn stack VM through B4, and the register path through R2. The register kernel, the stream linker, confinement, and the typecheck observer are designed and not yet built. Dependency closure and global distribution come after that. Where the two systems agree -- code as a nameless, hash-identified graph -- they agree closely. Where they differ, the difference is always the same one: Unison builds a guarantee into one system; \" [:code \"datom.world\"] \" turns it into an observer on a stream and pays for the generality in phases it has not finished.\"]\u001b[0m\n\u001b[031m-                   ]]]}\u001b[0m\n\u001b[032m+                   [:p \"Today yin.vm has the named source, the semantic VM, the projection and fingerprint, the De Bruijn stack VM through B4, and the register path through R2. The register kernel, the stream linker, confinement, and the typecheck observer are designed and not yet built. Dependency closure and global distribution come after that. Where the two systems agree -- code as a nameless, hash-identified graph -- they agree closely. Where they differ, the difference is always the same one: Unison builds a guarantee into one system; \" [:code \"datom.world\"] \" turns it into an observer on a stream and pays for the generality in phases it has not finished.\"]]]]}\u001b[0m\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc        | 60 ++++++++++++----------------\n src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc  |  5 ++-\n test/yang/python/antlr/publication_test.cljc | 40 ++++++++++++++++++-\n 3 files changed, 67 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)\nzsh:1: no matches found: src/cljc/yin/ast*\n;; :namespaces is disabled project-wide. It rewrites ns forms, which is\n;; unsafe on this multi-platform codebase in two distinct ways:\n;; 1. ClojureDart uses string-prefixed :import forms (e.g.\n;;    (:import [\"dart:core\" BigInt DateTime])); the rule rewrites these\n;;    into JVM-style forms, which the cljd compiler then fails to resolve.\n;; 2. .cljc files that guard a JVM-only :import/:require clause with\n;;    #?(:cljd nil :clj ...) rely on :cljd appearing FIRST (the cljd\n;;    host-eval pass also matches :clj, so first-match-wins order is\n;;    load-bearing — see the reader-conditional trap in project memory).\n;;    The rule reorders reader-conditional branches alphabetically\n;;    (:clj before :cljd), silently re-breaking the guard on every\n;;    `cljstyle fix` — this bit dao.jing.dht.node.cljc and cost a lost\n;;    commit before being traced back here.\n{:files {:extensions #{\"blog\" \"chp\" \"clj\" \"cljc\" \"cljd\" \"cljs\" \"edn\"},\n         :ignore #{\".cpcache\" \".git\" \".shadow-cljs\" \"node_modules\" \"target\"}},\n :rules {:blank-lines {:enabled? true, :max-consecutive 2},\n         :eof-newline {:enabled? true},\n         :indentation {:enabled? true},\n         :namespaces {:enabled? false},\n         :whitespace\n           {:enabled? true, :insert-missing? true, :remove-trailing? true}}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('test/yang/python/antlr/publication_test.cljc');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('''    (is (not (contains? vars 'try-require)))''','''    (is (not (contains? vars 'try-require)))\n    ;; Bundle installation evaluates only require and definitions. Mutable\n    ;; Python module state is allocated later, when a member body runs.\n    (is (= 5 (count (get-in bundle [:ast :operands]))))\n    (is (every? #(= 'yin/def (get-in % [:operator :name]))\n                (rest (get-in bundle [:ast :operands]))))\n    (is (= '#{m0-body m1-body}\n           (set (filter '#{m0-body m1-body} vars))))''')\ns=s.replace('''{:status :ok, :addresses {\\\"out\\\" :test/pym.out, \\\"a\\\" :test/pym.a, \\\"b\\\" :test/pym.b}}''','''{:status :ok, :addresses {\\\"out\\\" :test/pym.out, \\\"a\\\" :test/pym.a, \\\"b\\\" :test/pym.b},\n              :bundles {'pyscc.a\"'$$b :test/pyscc.a$$b}}'\"''')\ns+='''\n\n(deftest malformed-scc-member-names-test\n  (doseq [n [\\\"\\\" \\\".a\\\" \\\"a.\\\" \\\"a..b\\\" \\\"a\"'$b\"]]\n    (let [diagnostic (fn [f]\n                       (try\n                         (f)\n                         nil\n                         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo :cljs ExceptionInfo) e\n                           (ex-data e))))\n          expected {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                    :construct \"malformed module name\", :name n}]\n      (is (= expected (diagnostic #(lower/module-packet (:packet (unit n [])) {:name n}))))\n      ;; No packet is supplied: name validation must precede body lowering.\n      (doseq [units [[{:name n} {:name \"valid\"}]\n                     [{:name \"valid\"} {:name n}]]]\n        (is (= expected (diagnostic #(lower/scc-module-specs (h/registry) units :test/py {}))))))))\n\n\n(deftest bundle-refusal-stops-publication-test\n  (let [seen (atom [])]\n    (with-redefs [publish/publish-module!\n                  (fn [_ spec]\n                    (swap! seen conj (:name spec))\n                    {:status :refused, :reason :test/refused})]\n      (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :test/refused, :unit \"pyscc.a$$b\"}\n             (publication/publish-units! nil (h/registry) :test/py\n                                         [(unit \"a\" [\"b\"]) (unit \"b\" [\"a\"])\n                                          (unit \"later\" [])]))))\n    (is (= '\"'[pyscc.a\"'$$b] @seen))))\n'\"''';p.write_text(s)\nPY\nclojure -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.publication-test -n yang.python.antlr.import-test -e :slow > /tmp/c4-i5-r2-quick.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
