{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom zoneinfo import ZoneInfo\nnow=datetime.now(timezone.utc)\nheader=(f'Completed-GMT: {now:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT}\\\\n'\n        f'Completed-Local: {now.astimezone(ZoneInfo(\\\"Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\\\")):%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh}\\\\n'\n        'Coding-Agent: codex (gpt-6.1-sol)\\\\n'\n        'Session-ID: 01a14042-429f-7d21-a532-8cbd2bb7c468\\\\n')\nreport='''\n# Round 2 implementation findings\n\nImplemented the SCC lowering correction and both reviewer findings within the allowed source/test files. No linker or engine files changed. No commit or remote publication was made.\n\n- Removed bundle-time forward-reference cells and their enclosing lambda. Bundle installation now evaluates the prelude require followed by top-level \"'`yin/def` spec and body bindings. Sibling body deliveries read bare `mN-body` bindings in the bundle store; sibling specs remain literals and sibling `try-require` becomes `{:status :ok}`. Python runtime cells inside deferred bodies remain necessary for module state and are allocated only when those bodies execute.\n- Shared `validate-module-name!` between `module-packet` and `scc-module-specs`. SCC names are checked before sorting, bundle naming, or body lowering. Tests cover empty names, leading/trailing dots, `..`, and `$` in both member positions and compare diagnostics with singleton lowering.\n- Bundle publication refusal now reports string `:unit \"pyscc.<members>\"`; singleton and alias refusals retain Python name strings. The function docstring documents this shape, and a regression verifies refusal stops aliases and later units.\n- Fixed dotted sibling lookup discovered during review of the rewrite: mangled `pym.pkg$a` namespaces must map back to the original `pkg.a` member, rather than using `pkg$a` as a Python name. A regression checks sibling body bindings, literal specs, and retained parent deliveries.\n- Updated the deterministic bundle code fixture to `:segment/blake3-64f3647fb0c96ad0586848cb12492b568c11be5bae0f4eaaf7bc5e830d5f6653`, 103 rows (previously 109). Both alias code addresses and row counts remain unchanged.\n- Corrected an existing publication test expectation to include the returned `:bundles` entry.\n\n## Verification\n\nPASS: `clojure -M:test -n yang.python.antlr.publication-test -n yang.python.antlr.import-test -e :slow`\n\n```\nRan 27 tests containing 163 assertions.\n0 failures, 0 errors.\n```\n\nThe new quick `bundle-closures-lift-without-cells-test` executes installation and calls the real `engine/lift-slice` on all bundle exports on semantic, stack, and register VMs. All three halt, lift all four exports, and produce no `:cell-ref` values. This isolates installation by replacing only the prelude require with a literal nil; it does not claim full linked Python execution coverage. Existing quick initialization-lowering coverage passes.\n\nPASS: `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/publication_test.cljc` — 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n\nPASS: `mise exec -- cljstyle check src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc test/yang/python/antlr/publication_test.cljc`.\n\nPASS: `git diff --check`.\n\n`clj -M:kondo` alone exits 0 while printing usage; the explicit scoped lint above performs actual analysis.\n\nRepository-wide `mise exec -- cljstyle check` reports 26 existing incorrectly formatted files outside the edited files, including `bb.edn`, `deps.edn`, `shadow-cljs.edn`, public content, engine/encoder files, and the pre-existing untracked `debug_i5.clj`. They were left untouched under the file boundaries. The command also emits a mise cache write warning outside the workspace; scoped formatting still exits 0.\n\n## Remaining acceptance verification\n\nFull linked execution of the four guarded slow I5 execution tests, deterministic published SCC addresses, and Node/Dart lanes was not run on the laptop, per the brief. These remain for shiva verification. Thus the installation/lifting purity regression passes on all three vector VMs, but full linked SCC execution acceptance is not yet established by this report.\n\nExisting untracked prompts, logs, prior findings, and `test/yang/python/antlr/debug_i5.clj` were preserved. Session ID was verified against the provider `thread.started` record and `CODEX_THREAD_ID`.\n\n# Original task brief\n\n'\"'''\nprompt=Path('collab/1792079427542-engineer-c4-i5-r2.prompt.md').read_text()\nPath('collab/1792079427542-engineer-c4-i5-r2.findings.md').write_text(header+report+prompt)\nprint(header)\nPY\ncat /tmp/c4-i5-r2-kondo-scoped.log\ncat /tmp/c4-i5-r2-style-scoped.log\ngit diff --check\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
